      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_14739290525854a89c69a4f4f8333fbc61af86dd1c199f5696ea082544ce408e",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "For the displayed Rankin–Selberg product, taking logarithms exposes squared local power sums and exponentiation gives nonnegative Dirichlet coefficients. If that same Euler product has an established absolute-convergence boundary, Landau's theorem then turns the absence of coefficient cancellation at the boundary into one-sided bounds on every local root.",
