      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_164652e61635021345105ff9ab30930755b925ca6337f1f9a3fe7f5109b8627a",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "Petersson and automorphic trace formulas convert family averages of Hecke or Satake observables into an identity or diagonal main term plus geometric off-diagonal terms. The averaging weights are part of the induced family measure, so a weighted low-zero statistic need not estimate the unweighted counting-family density.",
