    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_3ad91f3fd497594e841853d61d34351d653260bc7472044a1f81a12ac75e253a",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "One-variable completion adds archimedean factors so a global L-function carries a reflection symmetry alongside its Euler-product data. In the multiple Dirichlet series, local correction polynomials instead place a cubic L-function d-sum and its reciprocal n-sum in one two-variable representation, allowing L-function reflection and quadratic reciprocity to act successively and transport residue data between polar loci.",
